# PR #456 Review

Severity levels: MUST-FIX, SHOULD-FIX, SUGGESTION

## Summary

Reviewed PR #456 ("'`fix: isolate doctor daemon tests from host environment`).

Checks performed:
- `gh pr diff 456`
- `gh pr view 456 --json title,body,files`
- `kspec task get @task-investigate-doctor-flaky-tests`
- `kspec task get @task-investigate-doctor-flaky-tests --json`
- `kspec validate` ✅ (passed)
- `pnpm vitest run tests/parser/doctor.test.ts` ✅ (29/29 passed)

Task trailer handling:
- PR body includes `Task: @task-investigate-doctor-flaky-tests`
- Task exists, but `spec_ref` is `null`
- Per instructions, skipped task spec AC and trait AC coverage checks

## Findings

### SHOULD-FIX

1. `tests/parser/doctor.test.ts:240`

The test under `ac-daemon-running` now explicitly mocks `getDaemonStatus()` as `running: false` and asserts the warning/not-running path. This preserves the flake fix, but it still does not exercise the actual "daemon running with PID" behavior implied by the AC name and top-level AC coverage comment.

Why this matters:
- A regression in the real running-state formatting (PID/port/uptime) can slip through even though `ac-daemon-running` appears covered.

Suggested fix:
- Either make this test simulate a running daemon (`running: true`) and assert PID/port/uptime fields/messages, or rename/re-annotate the test so it matches what it verifies.

## Posted Review

Posted via GitHub Reviews API as `COMMENT` with one inline comment on `tests/parser/doctor.test.ts` line `240`.
